  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BeO</mi></math> reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi></math> in presence of ammonia to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;which on thermal decomposition produces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and ammonium fluoride. Oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BeO</mi></math>&nbsp; on&nbsp;reaction&nbsp;with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi></math> in the presence of ammonia, &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is formed which on heating&nbsp;forms&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp; along with ammonium fluoride.&nbsp;<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BeO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>HF</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>heat</mi></mover><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p><p>Compound B is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>BeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;the&nbsp;oxidation state of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>",
